# ofclass — class handlers and if noun is ClassName: type check

kind living: alive, dead

verb shoot
    takes noun
    "Nothing to shoot."

class Person
    is animate.

    instead of examine:
        if dead:
            say "The person is dead."
        else:
            say "The person is alive."

class Animal
    is animate.

    instead of examine:
        say "It looks like an animal."

room Yard "A stone yard."

    instead of shoot:
        if noun is person:
            the noun is dead.
            say "The person falls."
        if noun is not person:
            say "That can't be shot."

    Person guard "A guard."

    Person prisoner "A prisoner."

    Animal dog "A dog."

test "class handlers"
    examine guard. "The person is alive"
    examine prisoner. "The person is alive"
    examine dog. "It looks like an animal"

test "ofclass"
    shoot guard. "The person falls"
    examine guard. "The person is dead"
    shoot prisoner. "The person falls"
    shoot dog. "That can't be shot"
